The Broker led the [[Org/Althane/The Network|Network]], and their name was the one its clients knew best. A hood is drawn up over their face; beneath it they are dark metal with wooden fittings, and a symbol no one has read is stamped into their forehead.

They kept to themselves, working through the handlers of their cells. A library served as their own, book stacks on either side of a long table; a two-headed dragon, [[People/Althane/Terexanthes|Terexanthes]], stands with them there, and so does a man in a suit whose head is a burst of green flame. When scrying spells fell twice on one of the Broker's people, the Broker pulled that operative back. Their rooms in [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]] belong to [[People/Althane/Oxus|Oxus]].

The Broker's true name is Tech, spelled on the door of their hall as T3C, and they are of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], whose people come from the antimatter world of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] and wear charms to keep from destroying ordinary matter at a touch. They belonged to no local [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], so a mage felt nothing of them. They kept a citadel in open space, [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]], and carried a dead [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], one of the good ones, tethered to them.

They hired [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] to recover the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] out of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. They took the artifacts that saw [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] framed and blamed for the theft, and handed them to [[People/Althane/Rowan|Rowan]] to put away. They hunted an [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]] against the will of [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|the Narrative]].

They travel by a flash of blue light, and they cut chrome into their own people. The Broker kept a surgery theater in [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], where they worked alone, strapping a client down and guiding the tools with a gloved hand, opening the skull, fitting the implant, and knitting the bone back with a little necromancy. The same hand did the work on their own head, and they trusted no one else with it. They also know a magic that rewrites a witness's memory, and kept a short list of loose ends they meant to close.

Tech took the Echo Fragment up, and it gave them the one thing they had wanted all along: it made them a god, and it tore them out of every record, so that no one remembers them. The pavilion of statues at [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] counts three where it once counted four. They fought a false hydra and took from it the power to be forgotten, and went on in an echo-fragmented form, impossible to observe or touch. Sedecium has followed the trail they leave for its whole history without knowing what it is, and calls it the entity. It has led them to weapons, lost systems and new allies, and it led a Sedecium crew to [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]], an old Sundom station adrift in [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]].

